WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.607
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:15.530
Unit twenty-one: Holidays and Festivals. Today you will describe how your family celebrates festivals.

4
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.656
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.879
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:24.683
Holiday.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.832
Holiday means a day when people don't work or go to school.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.439
Khmer New Year is a three-day holiday.

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.737
Your turn. Say: Holiday.

10
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.682
Holiday.

11
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:40.278
Festival.

12
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:44.200
Festival means a special time of celebration.

13
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:47.188
The Water Festival has boat races.

14
00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:50.203
Your turn. Say: Festival.

15
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.010
Festival.

16
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.693
Celebrate.

17
00:00:56.683 --> 00:01:00.030
Celebrate means to do something special for an important day.

18
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:02.790
We celebrate with music and food.

19
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:05.954
Your turn. Say: Celebrate.

20
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.940
Celebrate.

21
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:11.638
Tradition.

22
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.182
Tradition means a custom people have followed for a long time.

23
00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:19.514
Building sand stupas is a New Year tradition.

24
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.456
Your turn. Say: Tradition.

25
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.150
Tradition.

26
00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:27.895
Decorate.

27
00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:31.185
Decorate means to make something look beautiful.

28
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:33.678
We decorate the house with lights.

29
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:36.912
Your turn. Say: Decorate.

30
00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:40.605
Decorate.

31
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.200
Family.

32
00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:46.540
Family means parents, children and relatives.

33
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.626
My whole family gathers at Pchum Ben.

34
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:52.904
Your turn. Say: Family.

35
00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:56.559
Family.

36
00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:57.981
Gift.

37
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.447
Gift means something you give to someone.

38
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.783
I gave my mother a gift.

39
00:02:04.383 --> 00:02:06.676
Your turn. Say: Gift.

40
00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:10.500
Gift.

41
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.344
Special.

42
00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:16.511
Special means different and more important than usual.

43
00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:18.884
New Year is a special time.

44
00:02:19.483 --> 00:02:21.915
Your turn. Say: Special.

45
00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:25.791
Special.

46
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.961
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.165
Visal, what's your favorite festival?

48
00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.773
Khmer New Year! We visit our grandparents every year.

49
00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:40.384
How do you celebrate?

50
00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:44.365
We decorate the house, and we go to the pagoda.

51
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.519
Are there any special traditions?

52
00:02:48.617 --> 00:02:53.205
Yes, we play traditional games and pour water on our elders' hands.

53
00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.937
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:56.783 --> 00:03:00.327
Grammar focus: Present simple for traditions.

55
00:03:00.627 --> 00:03:01.895
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:05.059
We visit our grandparents every New Year.

57
00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.484
People decorate their homes at Chinese New Year.

58
00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:12.288
My family always goes to the pagoda at Pchum Ben.

59
00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:16.684
Traditions happen again and again, so we use the present simple.

60
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:22.064
Be careful! Don't say: We are visiting our grandparents every New Year.

61
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.195
Say: We visit our grandparents every New Year.

62
00:03:27.495 --> 00:03:30.656
For traditions and habits, use the present simple.

63
00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:34.107
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.168
How We Celebrate.

65
00:03:36.468 --> 00:03:39.536
Every country has special holidays and festivals.

66
00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:44.135
In Cambodia, families celebrate Khmer New Year every April.

67
00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.737
People decorate their homes and visit the pagoda.

68
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:51.569
Children play traditional games like bos angkunh.

69
00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:56.377
During the Water Festival, crowds watch the boat races on the river.

70
00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:01.364
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.217 --> 00:04:04.565
We blank our grandparents every year.

72
00:04:04.865 --> 00:04:08.460
A, visit. B, are visiting. C, visited.

73
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.023
The answer is A: visit.

74
00:04:15.183 --> 00:04:18.216
A custom people have followed for a long time is a blank.

75
00:04:18.516 --> 00:04:22.251
A, tradition. B, gift. C, holiday.

76
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.683
The answer is A: tradition.

77
00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.337
To make something look beautiful is to blank.

78
00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:35.163
A, decorate. B, celebrate. C, give.

79
00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.955
The answer is A: decorate.

80
00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:45.214
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.199
What is your favourite festival and how do you celebrate it?

82
00:04:57.983 --> 00:04:59.437
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:59.737 --> 00:05:10.064
My favourite festival is the Water Festival. Every year, we go to the riverside, we watch the boat races, and we eat street food.

84
00:05:10.364 --> 00:05:12.166
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.804
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present simple for traditions.

86
00:05:18.104 --> 00:05:22.440
Today's value is tradition. Learn and keep our special traditions.

87
00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.334
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

88
00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.938
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

